WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:04.420
Robert De Niro has some things to say about
the things other people are saying about his

00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:05.340
new movie.

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:09.580
We're talking of course of Todd Phillips'
Joker, the controversial new film from Warner

00:00:09.580 --> 00:00:13.660
Brothers and DC in which De Niro appears in
a major supporting role.

00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:18.039
Over the course of his decades-long career
in cinema, De Niro has played everything from

00:00:18.039 --> 00:00:23.050
hard-nosed gangsters and bullish boxers to
overprotective fathers and emotionally damaged

00:00:23.050 --> 00:00:24.050
war vets.

00:00:24.050 --> 00:00:28.240
He even threw down against a certain moose
and squirrel duo in a kid-friendly comedy.

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:30.100
"Are you talking to me?"

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:33.180
"No, I'm talking about you."

00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:34.560
"Well, I'm the only one here.

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:36.580
So you must be talking to me."

00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:41.300
This year, De Niro is charging right back
into the "for your consideration" fray with

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:43.240
the raw and gritty Joker.

00:00:43.240 --> 00:00:47.840
While the dark take on the Clown Prince of
Crime seems primed to set the box office on

00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:52.240
fire, Joker has also found itself wrapped
up in some surprising controversy.

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:57.700
The contention surrounds the rampant gun violence
that plays a part in Joker's story, with violence

00:00:57.700 --> 00:01:02.160
and firearms tending to accompany the Joker
character in whatever form he takes.

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:06.740
The perceived content of the movie has inspired
some family members of the victims of the

00:01:06.740 --> 00:01:11.570
2012 mass shooting in Aurora, Colorado, which
tragically unfolded during a screening of

00:01:11.570 --> 00:01:13.760
Warner Bros.

00:01:13.880 --> 00:01:17.520
The Dark Knight Rises, to pen a heartfelt
letter to the studio prior to Joker's release.

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:22.880
They say they're concerned that Joker may
inadvertently inspire copycat acts of violence.

00:01:23.080 --> 00:01:30.420
"This movie is really fueling the fire for
anyone who might even be thinking about being

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:32.420
a copycat of a mass shooter."

00:01:32.680 --> 00:01:37.540
The group further urged the studio to lobby
for gun reform, cease their support of public

00:01:37.540 --> 00:01:41.650
figures who advocate for gun rights, and to
consider throwing more support behind groups

00:01:41.650 --> 00:01:43.280
who help the victims of gun violence.

00:01:43.640 --> 00:01:49.579
"We wanted them to have civic responsibility,
corporate responsibility, and to do the right

00:01:49.580 --> 00:01:51.860
thing by survivors of gun violence."

00:01:52.060 --> 00:01:56.620
That letter has left Joker's director, cast,
and studio in the hot seat as they've been

00:01:56.620 --> 00:01:59.300
promoting the movie ahead of its October 4th
release.

00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:04.320
In the last week alone, Phillips, Phoenix,
and Warner Bros. have all opened up with their

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:06.780
own particular views regarding the matter.

00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:11.720
And now, chatting to Variety during the red
carpet event for another of his upcoming films,

00:02:11.720 --> 00:02:16.360
The Irishman, Robert De Niro finally offered
his own take on the Joker controversy.

00:02:16.360 --> 00:02:21.180
De Niro, who plays a talk show host named
Murray Franklin in the film, had this to say:

00:02:21.520 --> 00:02:22.980
"I know there's controversy.

00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:27.800
I think some of the things that were being
said about Warner Bros. giving money, not

00:02:27.800 --> 00:02:31.180
endorsing, or whatever it was about the NRA,
I think is right."

00:02:31.460 --> 00:02:36.060
De Niro's words about the Joker controversy
will hardly come as a surprise to folks who

00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:37.800
have followed his work in recent years.

00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:42.220
The actor's unflinching political perspectives
and open criticisms of the American government,

00:02:42.220 --> 00:02:46.280
and especially President Donald Trump, have
made him a target of politicians and other

00:02:46.280 --> 00:02:48.880
people who stand on the opposing side of those
views.

00:02:49.360 --> 00:02:51.540
"You've called him a bully, a pig.

00:02:51.540 --> 00:02:53.100
Threatened to punch him."

00:02:53.500 --> 00:02:54.260
"Um."

00:02:54.680 --> 00:02:59.340
Needless to say, it's probably a good thing
that he wasn't quite so frank in response

00:02:59.340 --> 00:03:02.220
to the Joker controversy as he's been about
other topics.

00:03:02.220 --> 00:03:07.000
De Niro wisely didn't use the moment to grandstand
or stump for his own views, instead simply

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:10.160
offering his own support of the Aurora families
and their worries.

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:14.840
As for the current controversy, the Joker,
despite always being shown as a homicidal

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:19.840
maniac, seems to inspire a sort of idol worship
mentality amongst his fans.

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:24.980
The character's rock-star-like aura seemed
to reach a new level with Heath Ledger's unforgettable

00:03:24.980 --> 00:03:27.920
turn as the clown in 2008's The Dark Knight.

00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:33.120
While the connections between that film and
the actions of the Aurora shooter remain tenuous,

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:36.720
many still believe the Joker served as inspiration
for the violent act.

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:41.820
As such, some also believe this new take on
the character may be dangerously provocative.

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:46.120
On the other hand, plenty of people see no
reason to worry about Joker at all, seeing

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:50.770
it as just another edgy comic book movie,
so this may go down as a case of much ado

00:03:50.770 --> 00:03:51.660
about nothing.

00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:55.960
There doesn't appear to be any movement to
stop Joker from being released, and the Aurora

00:03:55.960 --> 00:03:58.580
families haven't called for a boycott of the
film.

00:03:58.580 --> 00:04:03.360
They simply argue that if Warner Bros. is
going to profit off fictional gun violence,

00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:07.880
they would do well to treat the victims of
real gun violence with consideration and support.

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:13.260
Warner Bros. remains steadfast that Joker
in no way attempts to portray Joker as a heroic

00:04:13.260 --> 00:04:14.060
figure.

00:04:14.060 --> 00:04:18.600
Amidst the controversy, the studio is urging
people to withhold judgement until they've

00:04:18.600 --> 00:04:23.190
actually seen the film, with a spokesperson
recently offering, quote, "A lot has been

00:04:23.190 --> 00:04:26.900
said about Joker, and we just feel it's time
for people to see the film."

00:04:26.900 --> 00:04:31.340
As for De Niro, aside from the controversy,
he's had nothing but positive things to say

00:04:31.340 --> 00:04:33.260
about his experiences on Joker.

00:04:33.260 --> 00:04:34.600
As he told to Variety,

00:04:34.780 --> 00:04:37.520
"I like Todd Phillips and Joaquin.

00:04:37.520 --> 00:04:41.900
They're terrific to work with."

00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:47.060
With any luck, the energy surrounding Joker
will remain similarly positive, and the film

00:04:47.061 --> 00:04:51.590
will arrive with little more than a heady
dose of entertainment value, a dash of societal

00:04:51.590 --> 00:04:54.380
insight, and a stream of awards season success.

00:04:54.380 --> 00:04:58.800
But of course, we won't get a real sense of
how Joker plays until the film hits theaters

00:04:58.800 --> 00:05:00.160
on October 4th.

00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:02.760
Here's hoping there are happy faces all around.

